# C009: Re-entrant BoxedCall clears an outer invocation's live state
#
# CONFIRMED — static analysis (re-entrancy use-after-free / state corruption)
#
# BoxedCall_internal_call does not guard against re-entrancy:
#
#   if (0 == PyContext_Enter(self->context)) {
#       // ... execute the call ...
#       PyContext_Exit(self->context);
#   }
#   // falls through REGARDLESS of whether Enter succeeded
#   BoxedCall_clear(self);   // clears context + args, sets Dormant
#
# If re-entered during execution (e.g. through apsw.aio._tls.current_call.call
# or an argument __del__ triggered by the decrefs in BoxedCall_clear before
# call_type is set to Dormant), the recursive call clears the outer invocation's
# context and arguments.  The outer call then operates on cleared/freed state
# (PyContext_Exit on a Py_CLEAR'd context pointer).
#
# Runtime repro requires the full apsw.aio async machinery to arrange
# re-entrancy during a BoxedCall; the code path is unambiguous.
